# Exact Homebrew formula names that brew-sync must not write to the Brewfile as
# explicitly Homebrew-owned packages.
#
# These entries do not prevent Homebrew from installing a formula when another
# Brewfile package requires it as a transitive dependency. They also do not
# uninstall anything. Homebrew may therefore keep its own copy of Node, Python,
# Zig, or another excluded runtime while mise or uv supplies the development
# version that wins PATH precedence.
#
# Matching is exact; wildcards are not supported. Add versioned formulas
# separately when needed, for example `python@3.12` and `python@3.13`.
bun
go
node
python
python@3.12
rbenv
ruby
ruby-build
zig
zls
